# `link` (SPEC.md §19): a typed message contract callable both in-process
# and, via the generated `Greet_handler`/`Greet_remote` pair, from a
# separately-compiled CuNi program running as a *different* target — see
# tests/conformance.rs's `link_interop_go_server_python_client` for a real
# example of a Go-compiled server answering a Python-compiled client over an
# actual socket. Mounting the handler (starting an HTTP server, choosing a
# port) is the user's own job, per the ratified "codegen-only, no bundled
# runtime" decision (INTEROP_PROPOSAL.md item 6) — this file only declares
# the contract and its local implementation.
link Greet(name: str, times: int) -> str do
    ret `hello ${name} x${times}`
end
